<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3723" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arpi</span></b> , ōrum, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in Apulia</i>,
			earlier called Argyripa (q. v.), now <i>Arpa</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 11, 16, § 104</span></i>; cf. Mann. Ital. II. 82
			sq.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv.: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arpīnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>from Arpi</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dasius Altinius Arpinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					24, 45</span></i>
			; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arpīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Arpi</i>, <i><span class="en">id. 24,
			47</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ar-pānus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>pertaining to
			Arpi</i>, Front. Col.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arpāni</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., <i>the inhabitants of Arpi</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 11,
				16, § 103</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
